#####################################################################
USB GameCube Adapter (Wii U) v1.2 movable build, not yet console-tested [ausbigshow]
#####################################################################
# Lets the official Wii U GameCube Controller Adapter (WUP-028) work in game
# in Project+ 3.2.1 on vWii. Add to BOOST.txt with
#     .include Source/Extras/USBGameCubeAdapter-Movable.asm
# anywhere, with any other codes. Use either this or USBGameCubeAdapter.asm,
# not both.
# Don't also turn on the launcher add-on: it would be a second copy.
#
# Generated by build.py from src/entry.S and src/gca.c (the C lines are the
# "#|" comments; under -O2 they come out of order). Change the C and rebuild
# rather than editing this file. Source and docs:
# https://github.com/ausbigshow/pplus-gca-addon
#
# This is one C0 (PULSE) code that runs every frame:
# - The first run adds its own address to the absolute addresses in its
#   address table (.got2) and in the words listed after it (.fixup), so it
#   works wherever GCTRM places it.
# - On its first run gca_install finds the `bl PADRead` in
#   gfPadSystem::updateLowGC (0x80029578) and the `bl PADControlMotor`s,
#   checks their code signatures, and redirects them to gca_PADRead / gca_PADControlMotor below. If a
#   signature doesn't match it patches nothing.
# - From there it talks to the adapter through IOS /dev/usb/hid (v4 or v5).
#
# Status block for memory viewers: gca_diag is at code body + 0x1ecc
# (the C0 line + 8 + 0x1ecc); see the README
# for its twelve words.
# Size: 0x2788 bytes. Brawl addresses used are the #define ADDR_* lines in gca.c.

